# Part B — Core Domain Model and Business Rules

## Purpose
Implement all non-GUI logic for sessions, XP, medals, day attribution, streaks, and statistics.

This is the heart of the app and should be fully independent of CustomTkinter.

## Scope
- Define session model
- Implement XP calculation
- Implement medal calculation
- Implement day attribution
- Implement streak logic
- Implement stats calculations
- Implement all derived aggregate logic

## Core Model

### Session
A session will contain:
- unique id
- start local datetime
- end local datetime
- duration in minutes
- created-at local datetime
- source: preset/custom

## Business Rules to Implement

### XP Rules
- XP rate = `settings.xp_per_10_minutes`
- Default = 10
- XP only for completed 10-minute blocks
- Formula:
  - completed blocks = `duration_minutes // 10`
  - XP = completed blocks × XP rate
- No fractional XP

### Medal Rules
Daily medal is based on total study time for a calendar day:
- Bronze: at least 120 minutes
- Silver: at least 180 minutes
- Gold: at least 300 minutes
- Only highest medal counts/displayed
- Medal thresholds are inclusive

### Day Attribution Rules
- A session belongs to the calendar day of its **start datetime**
- Midnight-crossing sessions are not split
- Full duration and XP are assigned to start day

### Streak Rules
- A qualifying day = total study time for that day ≥ 10 minutes
- Current streak:
  - if today qualifies, count consecutive qualifying days ending today
  - if today does not qualify, count consecutive qualifying days ending yesterday
- Longest streak:
  - maximum consecutive qualifying days in saved history

### Statistics Rules
Need calculations for:
- Today XP / time
- This week XP / time
- This month XP / time
- Lifetime XP / time
- Current streak
- Longest streak
- Total sessions
- Active days
- Average daily study time
- Bronze count
- Silver count
- Gold count

### Period Definitions
- Today = current local calendar day
- Week = Monday through Sunday
- Month = current calendar month
- Lifetime = all sessions in current save data

## Tasks
1. Create session data model
2. Implement validation rules for session durations:
   - minimum 5 minutes
   - maximum 12 hours
   - hours 0–12
   - minutes 0–59
   - friendly validation messages supported by core result types
3. Implement session creation logic:
   - end = current local time
   - start = end − duration
4. Implement day attribution logic
5. Implement daily aggregate builder:
   - group sessions by start date
   - calculate total minutes and XP per day
6. Implement XP engine
7. Implement medal engine
8. Implement streak engine
9. Implement stats engine
10. Add unit tests for all core rules

## Recommended Test Cases
This part should include tests for:

### XP Tests
- 5 minutes = 0 XP
- 10 minutes = 10 XP
- 25 minutes = 20 XP
- 30 minutes = 30 XP
- 1 hour = 60 XP
- 2 hours = 120 XP
- 2 hours 9 minutes = 120 XP

### Medal Tests
- 119 minutes = no medal
- 120 minutes = Bronze
- 179 minutes = Bronze
- 180 minutes = Silver
- 299 minutes = Silver
- 300 minutes = Gold

### Midnight-Crossing Tests
- Session ending at 00:10 with calculated start on previous day belongs to previous day
- Session from 23:30 to 01:30 belongs entirely to start day

### Streak Tests
- 9-minute day does not qualify
- 10-minute day qualifies
- gap breaks streak
- current streak remains if today has not qualified yet but yesterday ended a valid streak

## Deliverables
- Fully testable core domain layer
- XP/medal/streak/stats engines
- Date-attribution logic
- No GUI coupling

## Acceptance Criteria
- All required core calculations work correctly
- Core can be used without CustomTkinter
- Unit tests cover all confirmed edge cases
- No derived values are stored as authoritative truth

